            <ArticleTitle>Aortic root abscess with coronary artery involvement: diagnostic and surgical management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>653-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe two cases of infectious endocarditis in infants complicated by aortic root abscess involving the coronary artery treated by the Ross operation. Multislice computed tomography was important in defining the diagnosis and in planning subsequent surgical management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
